  "answer_text": "As an AI, I cannot directly purchase tickets or process payments for you, but I can guide you through booking your train ticket from Boston to New York. \n\nSince today is **Sunday, June 7, 2026**, \"next Friday\" most likely refers to **Friday, June 12, 2026** (or **Friday, June 19, 2026**, if you are planning a week further out).\n\nA guide on your options, estimated prices, and how to book your round-trip ticket is detailed below:\n\n### 1. Choose Your Train Service\nAmtrak operates two main services between Boston (South Station or Back Bay) and New York (Moynihan Train Hall at Penn Station):\n*   **Amtrak Northeast Regional:** Takes about **4 hours and 15 minutes**. This is the most popular and budget-friendly option. \n*   **Amtrak Acela / NextGen Acela:** High-speed service taking about **3.5 hours**. It features only Business and First Class seats. \n\n### 2. Estimated Pricing \nBecause you are booking less than a week in advance for a peak travel day (Friday), fares are likely higher than average:\n*   **Northeast Regional (Coach):** Typically ranges from **$60 to $150+** one-way for last-minute weekend bookings.\n*   **Acela (Business):** Typically ranges from **$130 to $300+** one-way.\n\n---\n\n### How to Buy Your Return Ticket Instantly\n\n#### Option A: Book Directly on Amtrak (Recommended)\nBooking directly is usually the best option for flexible change and cancellation policies. \n1. Go directly to the **[Amtrak Official Website](https://www.amtrak.com)** or open the Amtrak mobile app.\n2. Set your origin to **Boston, MA - South Station (BOS)** (or Back Bay) and destination to **New York, NY - Penn Station (NYP)**.\n3. Select **Round Trip**.\n4. Input your dates:\n    *   **Departing:** `06/12/2026` (or `06/19/2026`)\n    *   **Returning:** Select your preferred return date (e.g., Sunday, `06/14/2026` or same-day Friday `06/12/2026`).\n5. Click **Find Trains** to compare times, choose your outbound and return trains, and complete your checkout.\n\n#### Option B: Compare and Book via Third-Party Search Engines\nIf you want to quickly compare Amtrak fares against regional bus options (like Greyhound or Peter Pan) to see if you can get a cheaper deal, you can use comparison platforms:\n*   **[Wanderu](https://www.wanderu.com):** A search tool specifically tailored for finding cheap train and bus tickets on the Northeast Corridor.\n*   **[Busbud](https://www.busbud.com):** Let's you compare train times and bus schedules side-by-side to find the lowest price.\n\n*Tip: If you are a student, senior, or military member, make sure to apply your discount code on the Amtrak checkout page to save up to 10\u201315% on your booking!*",
